<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Daehan buys 24,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Daehan buys 24,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daehan Flour Mills Co Ltd said on Wednesday it bought 24,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Mitsui and Co Ltd.  </p>
<p>A Daehan official said shipment was set for May 15-June 15 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>Traders said the purchase was split into four postions -- 11,000 tonnes of western white/soft white, 1,000 tonnes of western white (club minimum 15 percent), 2,000 tonnes of hard red winter (protein minimum 11.5 percent), and 10,000 tonnes of dark northern spring (protein minimum 14 percent).</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follow:</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat		   Tonne	Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p> Western White/Soft White   11,000	 $157.15</p>
<p> Western White		   1,000	 $158.00</p>
<p> Hard Red Winter		 2,000	 $180.20</p>
<p> Dark Northern Spring	 10,000	 $190.50</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
